    "scenesThatPass": [
      "CLARA: Auntie --\nMISS MARTIN: With my dyspepsia? Do you want to kill me?\nCLARA: Aren't you going to have any supper?",
      "CLARA: Oh.\nARLY: I've a message for you -- from Harolday.",
      "CLARA: We-el, not exactly moving in. You see...\nMISS MARTIN: Do you have to discuss our private affairs with every rag-tag-and-bobtail cow-person we meet, Clara?\nCLARA: Auntie!",
      "MISS MARTIN: We can do very well without it -- thank you. And you're keeping your lady friend waiting.\nARLY: I thought maybe you'd changed your mind again.",
      "CLARA: I don't know how I can ever thank you for trying to help me. I do appreciate it ever so much -- Don't think too harshly of me, will you -- I…\nARLY: She's lovely, isn't she? -- So sweet -- honest, and helpless.\nARLY: Pity you didn't fall in love with her, instead of me."
    ]
  },
